= Dawen Liang 

~~~
{}{img_left}{files/dawen.jpg}{Dawen Liang}{124}{140} \n
Email: {{<img src="files/email.png" alt="email" width="6%">}} \n

I am a member of technical staff at [https://x.ai/ xAI]. Before that, I was a research scientist at [https://www.netflix.com/ Netflix] and worked on personalization, policy learning, and LLM post-training. I completed my Ph.D. in the [http://www.ee.columbia.edu/ Electrical
Engineering Department] at [http://www.columbia.edu/ Columbia University], 
as part of the [http://labrosa.ee.columbia.edu LabROSA],
working with [http://www.ee.columbia.edu/~dpwe/ Professor Dan
Ellis] and [http://www.cs.columbia.edu/~blei/ Professor David Blei].
Prior to that, I completed my master's degree in
[http://www.cs.cmu.edu/~music/mat/index.html Music and Technology program] at
[http://www.cmu.edu/index.shtml Carnegie Mellon University], working with
[http://www.cs.cmu.edu/~rbd Professor Roger Dannenberg] in the
[http://www.cs.cmu.edu School of Computer Science], where I was part of the
[http://www.cs.cmu.edu/~music/ Computer Music Group]. 
~~~

== Papers

For the most up-to-date information please see my [https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=4c1ZNm4AAAAJ&hl=en Google Scholar] page.


== Miscellaneous
Here are some (very old) notes regarding some topics I found interesting. 
I wrote these just for fun (and I hope they can be useful to someone in the future).
Therefore, there might be mistakes/errors in these notes. 
If you find any problems, please let me know.

- [files/mle_biased.pdf A proof] that Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) is
  biased for variance estimator.
- [files/mat_deriv.pdf A note] that shows some useful properties for matrix
  derivative.
- [files/em.pdf Some technical details] for the Expectation Maximization (EM)
  algorithm.

